7.
Summary
The H&CD Office allows the citizens of Cheyenne to comment on the Community Development Block
Grant (CDBG) cycle multiple times throughout the process.  A final public hearing was held during the
City Council meeting on April 24, 2023, the last date written comments were accepted for inclusion in
the Annual Action Plan.
The City of Cheyenne’s Amendment to the Program Year 2023 Annual Action Plan begins with the
publishing of a public notice on June 26, 2024, announcing a 30-day comment period from June 28th to
July 28th, to include the use of CDBG recaptured funds for a proposed Lincoln Park Sidewalk and ADA
Upgrade Project. On July 3rd, the Housing & Community Development Advisory Council will hold a Public
Hearing for the AAP amendment and Lincoln Park project, providing an opportunity for citizen input. A
second public hearing, on July 22nd, will be announced at the July 3rd City Council meeting. During the
July 22nd City Council meeting, a public hearing will be held, allowing citizens to provide comments after
a staff report on the AAP amendment. Citizens will have until July 28, 2024, to comment on the AAP.
Information on public hearings, assistance with accessibility, how and where to access the amended
AAP, and where to direct comments will be made available in the Public Notices disseminated through a
City of Cheyenne press release, run in the local newspaper, posted on the City Website, and
Facebook. Any comments received will be reviewed and included in the final copy of the amended AAP.
Comments requiring a response will receive a response quickly, and consideration will be given to
substantive recommendations.
```

